---
title: Core utilities
description: Framework-agnostic TypeScript — text index, search, geometry, page themes, the PDF codec and paper analysis.
---

`svelte-pdf-mini/core` has no Svelte imports: use it in workers, on the server or in another framework.

| Module | Exports |
| --- | --- |
| Text index | `PageText` (`raw`, `norm`, `quadsFor`, `rectFor`, `textOf`, `offsetAtPoint`), `normalizeWithMap`, `quadsBounds` |
| Search | `searchPageText`, `compileQuery`, `matchSnippet` |
| Geometry | `pdfRectToViewport`, `quadToSvgPoints`, `pdfRectToPercent`, `clamp` |
| Destinations | `resolveDestination`, `listNamedDestinations`, `classifyDest` |
| Zoom | `fitZoom`, `nextZoomStep`, `ZOOM_STEPS` |
| Page themes | `pageThemes`, `paperColors`, `paperSwatches`, `paperHex`, `paperTheme`, `mixHex`, `invertLightness` |
| Rendering | `RenderScheduler`, `renderPageToCanvas`, `renderRegionToCanvas`, `releaseCanvas` |
| Annotations | the `Annotation` model, `defaultPalette`, `hitTest`, `reanchorAll`, `defaultKeymap`, `comboLabel` |
| PDF codec | `exportPdf`, `importAnnotations`, `annotationsToMarkdown`, `annotationsToJSON` |
| Papers | `analyzePaper`, `pdfjsPaperSource`, `parseReference`, `sectionAt` |
| Providers | `defaultCitationProvider`, `openAlex`, `semanticScholar`, `crossref`, `arxiv`, `chainProviders` |
| Messages | `defaultMessages`, `setMessages`, `formatMessage` |

```ts
import { analyzePaper, pdfjsPaperSource } from 'svelte-pdf-mini/core';
import { getDocument } from 'pdfjs-dist';

const doc = await getDocument(url).promise;
const paper = await analyzePaper(pdfjsPaperSource(doc));
console.log(paper.meta.title, paper.references.length);
```
